{"name":"Granite","hex":"#746a5e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Granite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island of South Australia.","A town in Colorado."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Granite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Granite","blocks":[{"text":"Granite is a coarse-grained (phaneritic) intrusive igneous rock composed mostly of quartz, alkali feldspar, mica and plagioclase. It forms from magma with a high content of silica and alkali metal oxides that slowly cools and solidifies underground. It is common in the continental crust of Earth, where it is found in igneous intrusions. These range in size from dikes only a few centimeters across to batholiths exposed over hundreds of square kilometers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Bianco_Sardo_Granit_mit_polierter_Oberfl%C3%A4che.jpg/330px-Bianco_Sardo_Granit_mit_polierter_Oberfl%C3%A4che.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granite","wikidata":"Q41177"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg/500px-Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg/1280px-Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg/500px-Granite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_%28rotated%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGranite_Rosa_Porri%C3%B1o_-_es_(rotated).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Granite